Subject: [PATCH] Write a network's mac_value to the configuration file

A network with mac_addr=3 uses the address in mac_value, which is read from the
configuration file, but SAVE_CONFIG left it out. After a restart the network
had mac_addr=3 and an all-zero address, and never connected. Write it with
mac_addr, as wpa_config_write_mac_value() would.
---
--- a/wpa_supplicant/config_file.c	2026-11-12 20:45:11.112624649 +0100
+++ b/wpa_supplicant/config_file.c	2026-11-12 20:45:11.122088077 +0100
@@ -949,6 +949,9 @@
 	STR(roaming_consortium_selection);
 #endif /* CONFIG_HS20 */
 	write_int(f, "mac_addr", ssid->mac_addr, -1);
+	if (ssid->mac_addr == WPAS_MAC_ADDR_STYLE_DEDICATED_PER_ESS)
+		fprintf(f, "\tmac_value=" MACSTR "\n",
+			MAC2STR(ssid->mac_value));
 #ifdef CONFIG_MESH
 	STR(mesh_basic_rates);
 	INT_DEF(dot11MeshMaxRetries, DEFAULT_MESH_MAX_RETRIES);
